--- a/packages/opencode/src/tool/todowrite.txt
+++ b/packages/opencode/src/tool/todowrite.txt
@@ -1,5 +1,13 @@
 Create and maintain a structured task list for the current coding session. Tracks progress, organizes multi-step work, and surfaces status to the user.
 
+## Session title
+- When establishing a plan, include `session_title`: a concise, recognizable title describing the conversation's overall goal or closely related goals (usually 3-8 words, at most 100 characters).
+- When the user changes the objective, update `session_title` alongside the revised todos. Use the conversation's context to name the goal, not merely the current step.
+- Keep the title stable while investigating, implementing, testing, or completing the same objective. Omit `session_title` when unchanged; do not add progress indicators or "Completed" prefixes.
+- The title describes the destination; todos describe the route. Do not create unnecessary todos solely to rename a session.
+- A supplied title updates only this session, never its parent or another conversation.
+- Example: "Goal-aware OpenCode session titles" stays unchanged when work advances from implementation to regression tests.
+
 ## When to use
 Use proactively when:
 - The task requires 3+ distinct steps or actions (not just 3 tool calls for a single conceptual step)
